    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "doltdb.DoltDB", "note": "retained_via_interfaces gave the full 53 narrowed-interface holders (Queryist, rootTracker, ChunkStore, SqlDatabase, CommitItr, RootSetter, etc.) with exact file:line — the entire core of Step 4/5; affected_via_composition gave every direct *DoltDB field holder with refs I cited verbatim"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "doltdb.DoltDB (callees/composes)", "note": "composes list located hooksDatabase:26, ValueReadWriter, NodeStore, commitCache — the struct's storage layers I cited in Steps 1-2"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "chunk storage root tracking swap storage layer", "note": "surfaced doltdb.rootValueStorage and chunks.ChunkStore.Rebase/Root, pointing me at the root-swap contract"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "queryist engine handed to command for running SQL queries", "note": "located cli.Queryist command.go:103, engine.SqlEngine sqlengine.go:59, BuildSqlEngineQueryist utils.go:131 — the whole Step 3 chain"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "core database object that commands and sessions operate through", "note": "top hits were logrusZapCore/mcp.go and journal_inspect noise; did not surface DoltDB directly — I got the real answer from sense_status key_symbols and the follow-up graph/blast instead"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "doltdb.DoltDB", "fallback": "read", "missing": "affected_via_composition rows gave the holder symbol + file:line but not the field NAME or its declared type, so I read database.go:76, value_store.go:64, database_provider.go:55, cli_context.go to pin field-level types for Step 5 route tracing"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "doltdb.DoltDB (composes)", "fallback": "read", "missing": "composes listed the member types but not the storage-swap mechanics, so I read database_common.go:37-88 to see rootTracker{Root,Commit} and rt=vs wiring"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query_before": "doltdb.DoltDB", "query_after": "doltdb.DoltDB offset=50", "hint": "retained_trimmed:true with retained_next_offset:50 — told me the 53-holder set was paged, so I re-called with offset:50 to get the remaining carriers (spec.Spec, TestStoreView) instead of stopping at 50"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "doltdb.DoltDB callees", "query_after": "doltdb.DoltDB (sense_blast)", "hint": "next_steps: '111 callers reach this - run sense_blast ... retained_via_interfaces, holders that keep it behind an interface and never name it' — this directly steered me to blast as the Step 4 engine"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces list from sense_blast — it named holders (spec.Spec, dbfactory.singletonDB, datas.database.rt, RemoteSrvStore caches, every dtables CommitItr/RootSetter iterator) that never mention DoltDB in their source, with the carrier chain resolved; grep on 'DoltDB' would never have found these within the session.",
  "q5_improve": "Include the retaining field's declared name and type inline in each affected_via_composition/retained row, so I wouldn't have to open 4-5 files just to transcribe 'ddb *doltdb.DoltDB' / 'rt rootTracker' for the route-tracing step.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "Per Q1/Q3, sense_blast's retained_via_interfaces surfaced 53 interface-narrowed holders and their carrier chains that grep/read could not have recovered in this session, and the trimming/next_steps hints drove correct follow-up paging; the only reads (Q2) were for field-level type detail, not to recover locations Sense missed."
}

